  tri jobs-lesson "H" "B" — record a lesson in correspondence-crm/LESSONS.md
  tri tg-unread / tg-dialogs [N] — telegram: unread / chats (read only)
  tri tg-msg <chat> [N] / tg-search <text> [N] / tg-who
  tri game            — game loop for t27.ai/#/queen: state (iteration, tasks, findings)
  tri game-claim / game-release — loop lock (exit 75 = another run holds it)
  tri game-iterate    — new cycle: counter + last_run
  tri game-verdicts — Queen's verdicts on the public board + every ARMED bee PR on t27 checked for her accept at its head (exit 1 = rule broken, 2 = could not check)
  tri game-site [--force|--self-test] — can trinity main build t27.ai? runs the publisher's own prebuild:ci + check:silicon in a loop-owned worktree, cached per main SHA (exit 1 red, 2 could not check)
  tri trinity-report BODY.md [--pr N] [--head SHA] — run trinity's OWN work-report validator on a PR body before pushing (from a trinity checkout; exit 1 = CI would fail)
  tri game-writers [DAYS] — who wrote t27.ai (ghashtag.github.io) in the last DAYS (7): each commit named by its door (publisher, deploy-site, book-bot, hand, hand-gHashTag); exit 1 on an UNKNOWN door
  tri game-served [--all] — do t27.ai's llms.txt/agents.t27 match the trinity commit the apex names as its source? --all lists every top-level public file; exit 1 on drift
  tri game-vault [--check|--list|--accept PATH|--restore PATH [--from SNAP]|--self-test] — content-addressed snapshots of the loop's skill dir + tri itself (~/.cache/queen-loop/vault); save runs only when --check finds no loss
  tri blog list|check [slug]|lint|preview <slug>|build|live <slug> [--repo DIR] — the t27.ai blog (trinity apps/website): receipt states, caveats, an HTML preview of a draft with its tables and figures, tsc+vite
  tri blog gif record CAST -- "cmd"... | render CAST GIF [--max-idle S] [--colors N] — real commands in a pty to an asciicast, then a GIF (silences shortened and labelled in-frame)
  tri game-blog [--self-test] — does every post in t27.ai's served Blog chunk have its /blog/<slug>/ page and og-blog card on the apex? (verify-site.sh's predicate, asked between publisher runs); exit 1 on drift
  tri game-cadence [N] — the apex publisher's real cadence vs its */15 cron: fired-slot %, gap median/p99/max, run time, hand dispatches
  tri game-selftest [-v] — run every queen-game-loop script's --self-test (found by grep, not a list); exit 1 if any fails
  tri game-tick [--self-test] — one loop tick: run the anomaly scan and print only what changed since the last (NEW red / CLEARED / one standing line); exit 1 on a NEW red row
  tri game-merged [N] — audit the PAST: every merged queen-* PR on t27 against her verdict; flags DELETES-MOST merges (a gutted file). Exit 1 = merges without her accept
  tri t27-tri ARGS — run t27's own Rust tri (newest built target/*/tri), e.g. `tri t27-tri now add ...`; t27 hooks must not find this tri
  tri game-anomalies [--heal] — live checks: endpoints, apex vs main, publisher, chunk; --heal repairs
  tri game-next       — top open backlog task
  tri game-task ID [--title|--status|--note|--force] / game-finding "T" [--severity] / game-gate ID [--result]
  tri game-dash [open] — DASHBOARD.md + dashboard.html (Claude Code design); last step of a cycle
  tri game-report [N] — latest cycle report (first N lines)
  tri game-ingest J [--cycle N] — merge the workflow plan from journal.jsonl into the backlog (idempotent)
  tri game-lesson "H" "B" — record a lesson in queen-game-loop/LESSONS.md
  tri game-lessons [WORD...] — index of queen-game-loop lessons (no words), or the lessons containing ALL the words; exit 1 on no match
  tri game-wire [board|status|hardware|activity|research] — what the public endpoints actually carry (fields on N cards)
  tri game-prove MARKER | --entry index-X.js | --apex [--after index-OLD.js] [--minutes 9] — wait until t27.ai serves the Queen chunk with the marker / the named entry / the entry from the apex index.html (different from --after); exit 0 = proven
  tri game-gates [fast|full] [LOG] — the Queen gate chain (full = + 5 headless-Chrome contracts, ~8 min); exit 0 = all green
  tri game-ship BRANCH TITLE MSGFILE BODYFILE -- PATHSPEC... — add by pathspec, commit, push, PR, squash-merge, publisher dispatch (no watch and no prove)
  tri game-close TASK_ID "msg" — close a cycle: task done, anomalies --heal, closed_at, iterate, dash, release, skill commit (the report and CONTEXT.md are edited by hand BEFORE)
  tri game-spike [--no-build] — engine measurement on the current checkout: canvas2D vs Babylon, rAF p50/p95/p99, vsync misses, chunk brotli (GPU via ANGLE/Metal)
  tri game-local [--build|--stop] — "run it locally": vite preview of the built site on 127.0.0.1:4173 and open #/queen in the default browser (not in the app panel: the page is hidden there and the engine stalls)
  tri game-models [list|pull <slug>] — field models (public/queen/models) with sizes and licence; pull fetches a Kenney pack by slug only after the user says so, printing source and size
  tri game-objects [--json] — field object inventory: what is drawn, on which layer, and which entity stands behind it
  tri game-foundation [--out PATH] [--repo R] [--limit N] — GitHub snapshot for the foundation (closed issues, epics with children and ring, releases, rings) into public/queen/foundation.json; writes only when the content without generatedAt changes, otherwise prints unchanged
  tri game-plan [path] — module building plan from modules.json, by the same pure function that draws the field (core, scale, height, wings, antennas, rotation, hash)
  tri game-verify     — self-check of the game loop state: duplicate ids, unknown statuses and severity, stale lock (exit 1 = the state contradicts itself)
  tri game-status [API] — what the status pill and the VERDICTS tile read: swarmState, scheduler, dispatches (running/unreviewed), last tick decision
  tri game-round [API] — whether the Queen ticks: lastRoundAt and roundSeconds against the SERVER CLOCK (Date header), not the laptop
  tri game-clock [API] — whether the status endpoint exposes its clock to the browser on t27.ai (Date, Access-Control-Expose-Headers) and the skew against this machine
  tri game-bees [API] — live bees from public-board and the age of each one's last word on the activity wire against the round length (warm/COLD)
  tri game-events [KIND] [HOURS] [API] — recent events of one kind on the activity wire with their state, in INTEL FEED words (default: review)
  tri game-feed [HOURS] [API] — what the INTEL FEED header should say about a fresh wire response: rows, span between oldest and newest, kinds
  tri game-activity [HOURS] [API] — sample of /queen/public-activity over N hours: kinds, review verdicts by (issue, state) with all stamps, fresh tick
  tri game-measure NAME [--build] — run ONE headless contract qa/queen-NAME-contract.mjs on the current dist (refuses while the gate chain runs: dist is shared)
  tri game-contract NAME "what it proves" — create qa/queen-NAME-contract.mjs from the pick harness, register check:queen-NAME and append it to the full gate list (the tail fails ON PURPOSE)
  tri game-bar        — column widths of the resource bar at four desktop sizes in both languages (the measurement that found the 200 px brand brow)
  tri game-copy KEY [KEY...] — English and Russian value of a COPY key from Queen.tsx and how many places use it
  tri game-branch NAME — first action of a cycle: fetch origin and branch NAME from origin/main in the trinity checkout (refuses if the tree has foreign edits)
  --- continuous loop (trios) ---
  tri iter / iter-dash / iter-log [N] / iter-anchors — loop state, dashboard, log
  tri iter-render [--work f.json] — measure the swarm, update the anchors, redraw the dashboard
  tri iter-unlock — release the loop lock (only if `tri iter` says stale)
  tri swarm — live Queen state in one line
  tri fence — which paths stuck jobs hold (boundaries to avoid)
  tri brief-gate <draft.md ...> — check a task draft with the Queen's own parser
  tri facts [--record|--facts]    — measured dashboard numbers; what cannot be measured shows as '-'
  tri failures [--since N|<step>] — which chain steps fail, how often, and with what evidence
  tri channel                     — whether the single channel into the container is alive
  tri share-modules [--share]     — one dependency install, linked into every tree
  tri reap-finished [--reap]      — remove trees whose work is already published (by age, not by pressure)
  tri rescue [--rescue]           — rescue work a bee did not commit before it gets wiped
  tri container                   — who is PID 1 and how close to process exhaustion
  tri two-views [--record|--report] — whether /health and the ssh gateway agree at the same moment
  tri salvage <N> [--brief]       — what survived from a stale branch: names missing from the base; --brief writes a task
  tri proven [--by-source]        — whether fresh work proves anything; --by-source: split by kind of work
  tri coverage [--fresh]          — what share of accepted verdicts the audit can check (cache: 10s vs 217s)
  tri verdict-audit <N ...> | --accepted — check a bee's claimed verdict against its diff
  tri boundary <N ...>            — what a bee was allowed to touch and what it touched; CREATED vs edited
  tri t27-gen                     — regenerate ring T27-00 from .t27 (the artifact is not edited by hand)
  tri t27-parity                  — whether the generated ring and its handwritten production twin agree
  tri forked-files                — a file that lives in two places must not start saying different things
  tri ci-diff <run|--pr a b>      — which CI failures are NEW and which were red before you
  tri exposure                    — what the live service serves to an origin it does not know
  tri flaky [N|<run-id>...]       — which red tests fail ALWAYS and which only sometimes
  tri accept-rate                 — whether a brief that CAN fail gets accepted less often
  tri unverdicted [--limit N]     — dispatches with no VERDICT block: review will never judge them
  tri silent-loop [--limit N]     — attempts that do not spend the retry limit: the loop has no ceiling
  tri rejudge [--state S]         — a verdict the current code would no longer repeat (agreement ≠ correctness)
  tri agree [--pair NAME]         — two implementations of one rule on real rows: where they diverge and which way
  tri idle [--hours N]            — how long the swarm stood idle and what blocked the rounds (golden rule)
  tri unwired [--all]             — a gate that is written but that nobody runs
  tri reach [--since D] [--floor N] — which step of the heal chain GETS TO run and which is always last
  tri reap [--reap] — worktree collection at 80/60 thresholds, no --force
  tri lease [--release] — claim lease with an idle timer, retry cap 2
  tri heal [--dry] — all swarm repairs in one chain, in the right order
  tri author [--file] — open an issue from a measured shortfall, limit 5 open
  tri loop-selftest — calibration of the loop's own instruments (no network; the run prints the count, not this line)
  tri judge-packet <N ...> | --unauditable — build a packet for a judge to read
  tri needs-you [--all] — what waits for a human and how long it has waited
  tri loop-coverage — which loop tools have never run their live branch
  tri trend [hours] — rate of the counters, not their level
  tri clocks — which fields decisions hang on, and whether someone rewrites them
  tri fields [file] — whether code reads fields the query does not select
  tri fp-check [N] — whether the checkers accuse known-good work
  tri push-work [--push] — push bee branches that are missing on the remote
  tri close-done [--close] — close issues with accepted work (leaves epics alone)
  tri unpark [--release] — lift a retry cap spent on silence rather than work
  tri stale-escalations [--release] — release an escalation whose cause no longer reproduces
  tri holds — what the swarm holds now and whether two dispatches claim one file
  tri queue — queue depth (not the open count): what nobody has started yet
  tri latency — where the time goes: review vs bee work, and how many tasks per hour
  tri reap-local [--reap] — remove merged and clean worktrees from the laptop disk
  tri verdicts [hours] — share accepted, returned and unjudged: health, not load
  tri why [--all] — why the swarm is stalled: cause, evidence and what to do about it
  tri feed [--act] — feeding only: push, close, open, no audits
  tri mix — what KIND of work the swarm is doing: load and acceptance will not show it
  tri land [--land] — land accepted work left on branches outside the base
  tri ab <a> <nA> <b> <nB> — whether the difference stands out from noise, or there is just too little data
  --- cycle: measure, cross-examine, draw, record ---
  tri cycle [--deep] — one pass: measure, anomalies, dashboard, log entry (exit 2 = anomalies found; that is an answer)
  tri cycle-repair — the same plus the listed safe repairs (a dead owner's lock, CLEAN trees)
  tri cycle-dash — show the latest dashboard, with its filesystem age as the first line
  tri cycle-html — the same measurement, but wide: every number shows the command that measured it, and every anomaly has its repair next to it. Exit 2 if the measurement is older than one cycle
  tri cycle-anom [N] (alias: tri cycle-anomalies) — every anomaly in full: claim, truth, repair (the dashboard fits seven)
  tri cycle-sense [--deep] — measure only, no drawing
  tri cycle-log [N] — pass log: how many anomalies, which ones lingered, what was repaired
  tri cycle-note did|next "text" — prose is written by hand; the dashboard draws a blank if nobody wrote it
  tri cycle-doctor — whether everything the loop needs is in place, and whether every one of its commands is reachable
  tri driver — whether anyone is driving iterations at all. Exit 1 — no driver (a measured zero), 2 — could not read (this is NOT zero)
  tri drift [--adopt] — whether this is the file the timers run, and whether it is in the repository
                     (exit 1 — measured drift, 2 — could not read; --adopt by hand only)
  tri backlog — what the backlog CONTAINS, read issue by issue, not inferred from skip counters
  --- xilinx7 MVP loop (bitstream back half as .t27, skill xilinx7-bitstream-loop) ---
  tri x7-claim [who] / x7-release — fire lock (exit 75 = held by another fire)
  tri x7-audit [--heal] — spec tests, generated .rs vs .t27 (content), bitwalk CRC 12/12 + frame ECC 32520/32520 on Vivado refs,
                     FAR walk 32520 frames + 72 empty pads, pin sweep 82/82, segbits sweep 4224/4224, far.t27 part table drift,
                     stale lock (exit 2 = anomalies; --heal regenerates .rs, rebuilds bitwalk, drops stale lock)
  tri x7-mutate [SPEC] — mutation catalogue: every defect must fail the spec tests AND the Vivado sweep
  tri x7-writer [--heal] — bitwalk --write byte-identical to xc7frames2bit on ~/.cache/x7/writer (16 entries) + wrong-part refusal
  tri x7-fasm [--heal] — bitwalk --fasm byte-identical to fasm2frames on ~/.cache/x7/fasm (20 entries: 13 real, 5 synth, 2 refuse) + --strict
  tri x7-board build|compare|load|receipts|all — bitwalk on a real 200T build: byte-compare + timing vs openXC7, SRAM load (--owner-yes), harness receipts
  tri devkit flow|impact — the FPGA flow layer by layer: per-layer time, t27 replacements byte-compared, Amdahl ceilings, hours/yr
  tri cast record|render|card|check|scrub|html|add|publish|gallery — terminal recordings: real commands → .cast → GIF, X/OG card, t27.ai/term/<id>/ share page (publish archives to ~/skills/_state/casts/)
  tri x7-part [--print|--write] — far.t27 part table vs prjxray-db part.json (exit 1 = drift; --write regenerates it)
  tri x7-status / x7-next / x7-task ID [--status S] [--note N] / x7-lesson "H" "B" / x7-bench [N] / x7-refs
  --- AX7203 board (tern_tc: receipts, UART, formats) ---
  tri fpga            — where the UART is (behind a hub or direct), openocd, latest runs, git, loop
  tri fpga-status — USB (UART behind a hub?), openocd, lock, what is loaded (from the latest flash log), latest runs (verdict or exit), git
  tri fpga-audit [--heal] — anomalies: key in logs, log > 1 MB, unfinished log, a "verified" count
                     in a document with no log, uncommitted/unpushed records, two openocds,
                     stale lock (exit 2 = anomalies; --heal only clears a stale lock)
  tri fpga-claim [who] / fpga-release — loop iteration lock (exit 75 = held by another)
  tri fpga-run NAME -- COMMAND... — one board run into board_runs/NAME.log with the standard wrapper;
                     never overwrites an existing log (one attempt, both runs on record)
  tri fpga-keycheck [FILE...] — how many times the key occurs in each file (prints counts, never the key); no FILE = every board_runs/ and rehearsal_runs/ log, also flags logs >= 1 MB
  tri fpga-push trinity-fpga|igla-coder-gpu — fetch, rebase, key check of the outgoing patch,
                     push with the gHashTag token (HANDOFF section 9), no force
  tri fpga-usb / fpga-next / fpga-task ID [--status S --note N] / fpga-lesson "H" "B"
  tri fpga-usb — CP2102N placement: DIRECT/HUB by the locationID rule, cross-checked by the hub-class walk of uart_loss_hubfree_ax7203.py --usb (exit 1 = HUB, 3 = the two rules disagree)
  tri fpga-wire BAUD... — what the CP2102N actually sends (24 MHz / N) and which requested range
                     gives the same wire rate; a sweep step finer than that range measures nothing
  tri fpga-cost --top T --src F... [--param K=V1,V2] — LUT/FF/CARRY4/DSP/BRAM (B36+B18) under four synth_xilinx
                     flag sets and the spread of the difference: a gap below the spread is the mapper, not the design;
                     BRAM is how an inferred RAM is proven to have inferred (FF inflation means it did not)
  tri fpga-rehearse NAME -- COMMAND... — a no-board rehearsal twice at once into rehearsal_runs/NAME_{1,2}.log; refuses --port, /dev/, the key file, openocd; exit 0 only if both pass with the same events (wall-clock times masked). --compare LOG1 LOG2 compares two logs
  tri fpga-quiet [--per-cpu 2] [--wait S] [--hold 120] — wait until the 1-min load stays <= X per cpu for HOLD s; exit 0 quiet, 1 if WAIT passes first; starts nothing. Run it before a one-attempt board run
  tri fpga-prcheck BODY.md --repo OWNER/REPO [--fork OWNER/REPO] — before a PR: bare #N refs, the Claude Code trailer, estimated stamps, and a fork behind with workflow changes the token cannot push; exit 0 ready, 2 not; posts nothing
  tri fpga-hostnet IP — before a LAN run: the route to IP is direct on a local interface (no gateway, no VPN tunnel), IP is in its subnet and not this Mac, no ARP entry yet; exit 0 ok, 2 stop; sends nothing
  tri fpga-steps KEY [--plan FILE] — where a pre-registered board sequence stands (default plan NODE_ETHERNET_PLAN.md, e.g. KEY=E3; FILE is looked up here, then in conformance/; KEY is the start of the heading, e.g. "The board run" --plan UART_LOSS_HUBFREE.md): each tri fpga-run/-flash line against its board_runs log, commands that differ from the plan, out-of-order logs, the next step; prints only, runs nothing, judges nothing; exit 2 on a problem
  tri fpga-rxer — E3 RX_ER cases in simulation (conformance/eth_rxer_bench.py, about 4.5 min at nice 19): the pinned TB, model and RTL compiled unchanged plus formal/eth_rxer_inject.v as a second top that forces RX_CTL at one falling RXC edge; expectations fixed in NODE_ETHERNET_PLAN.md; exit 1 if any case disagrees. --gate also runs each case on the yosys netlist (the runner's gate_netlist) and requires every INJ/RXE/TXF/TB/UART| line of the gate log to equal the RTL log; each gate run took 28 to 30 min at nice 19 under load (15/15 at 22:35Z, 91b07fd86). Rerun after any E3 RTL change
  tri fpga-txhold [--self-test] — E3 TX hold and setup at the TX output buffers in nextpnr-xilinx's own SDF of the routed e3z (conformance/e3_tx_hold_model.py; spec specs/trinet/e3_tx_hold_model_ax7203.t27): with no argument prints the one recorded run (conformance/model_runs/e3_tx_hold_model.log) if it exists, else runs it once (about 2.5 min, needs /tmp/trinet-node-build/e3z); exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 NO VERDICT. PASS 23:23Z 2026-09-27: smallest hold 3445 ps on TXD1, bench 3000; the model has no clock skew. Another build or RTL needs its own spec
  tri fpga-rxcap [--self-test] — E3 RX capture at the RX flip-flops in the same SDF (conformance/e3_rx_capture_model.py; spec specs/trinet/e3_rx_capture_model_ax7203.t27; reads /tmp/e3txhold, pinned by sha, runs no tool): with no argument prints the one recorded run (conformance/model_runs/e3_rx_capture_model.log) if it exists, else runs it once (seconds); exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 NO VERDICT. PASS 00:21Z 2026-09-28: falling-edge hold 10900 ps on rxctl_n; RXC 2.4 ns behind its data through the BUFG, so rxd_p1 and an RX_ER nibble sample the new value over x -2.5..+0.5 ns (board ed should stay 0)
  tri fpga-tmpcheck [--archive] [--restore] | --self-test — every file a .t27 spec pins by sha256 under /tmp (emptied at boot): ok / CHANGED / GONE and whether a kept copy exists in trinity-fpga/artifacts/model_inputs/blobs (gitignored; MANIFEST.tsv tracked). --archive keeps present files, --restore puts kept ones back where gone (never over a CHANGED file); fpga-audit flags lost and unkept inputs and --heal does both. Exit 0 all kept, 1 some unkept or unlocated, 2 a pin lost
  tri fpga-decode LOG --tokenizer FILE [--model FILE] | --self-test — the board ids of a generation log as text; refuses unless every receipt verified, exit 0, board ids = CPU_INT_IDS, the model sha is the generation spec's and the tokenizer vocabulary equals the model's (the local results/step2 tokenizer is 32000, the model 8192: refused)
  tri fpga-runlog [NAME] [--tail N] [--watch S] — one command for a run's progress: grammar-parsed status of a live (polls) or finished board_runs log; --self-test
  tri fpga-budget [NAME] | --self-test — wire budget of a finished generation run: request and answer streams in bytes and seconds-alone, each share of the wall clock, in-run jobs/s against the link ceiling, request-bound or answer-bound verdict; REQ_LEN/RESP_LEN/BAUD come from the spec the log cites (the decode chain, stopped at the first spec pinning them), retransmit frames counted into the request stream and labelled approximate; refuses a live, short-verified, elapsed-less or constant-less log
  tri fpga-watch-clients NAME [--every 30] [--max 5400] — sample IOKit user clients on the CP2102N into board_runs/NAME.clients.log while board_runs/NAME.log is open; passive (ioreg only, never the UART lock); start it just before tri fpga-run NAME
  tri fpga-hole LOG... — UART hole size from nonce arithmetic (expected = 0x10000 + verified; every hex header must give the same number), not by eye
  tri fpga-ioclients — who holds IOKit user clients on the CP2102N (pid, count, alive) and which driver is bound (AppleUSBSLCOM or a vendor one); every fpga-run header gets "# usb clients" and "# usb driver" lines
  tri fpga-tristate FASM... — pads whose output enable comes out inverted (OLOGIC pad pip or routed T1 input without ZINV_T1; exit 1); the archived nextpnr-xilinx drops that bit under router1
  tri fpga-batch — the batched wire protocol design gate: conformance/tern_tc_batch_model.py --self-test (BatchCell reference model of specs/trinet/tern_tc_batch_ax7203.t27 — SETX/DOT6 frames, the RAM-read preimage rule, negative controls incl. RAM drift after SETX); exit 0 PASS
  tri fpga-batch-rehearsal — the batched protocol's job stream: conformance/tern_tc_batch_runner.py --self-test (26 checks — whole passes pipelined through one window, mixed 19/24-byte answers shaped by issued nonces and settled by tag — natural y-nonce collisions hit ~1% of DOT6 frames and resolve without a false stop, loss recovery over RxLoss/TxLoss/the hunting parser, zero-plane skip, per-row recombination vs the int8 oracle, the honest/corrupt rehearsal pair); exit 0 PASS
  tri fpga-batch-cosim [--passes wq|both] [--keep DIR] — conformance/tern_tc_batch_rtl_cosim.py: the rehearsal's
                     recorded request stream replayed through formal/tern_tc_layer_rtl_tb.v under iverilog
                     vs a fresh HuntingBatchCell (byte-for-byte; negative control = blind 24-byte framing).
                     Pre-built red: FAILs on the current core at the first SETX tag (no SETX/DOT6 ops yet);
                     PASS is the TERN_TC_BATCH_RTL_PLAN.md core edit's gate. The walk_answers precondition
                     refuses non-adjudicable streams (out-of-range phantom frames: model drops, RTL will
                     answer) loudly instead of reporting a mystery diff; needs iverilog+vvp
  tri fpga-specs — every conformance/*_from_spec.mjs --check: .t27 specs compile, test blocks pass, generated files have not drifted (exit 2 = drift)
  tri fpga-loopcheck — the standing per-fire sweep in one call: git status (informational), specs, keycheck, audit, one greppable verdict line; exit is the OR of the three real components
  tri fpga-repin FILE... [--check] — propagate a sha256 change of FILE through the pin graph to a fixpoint: leaf pins, cross-spec pins, params regeneration, params pins. Never guesses: a missing pinned file is skipped with a note, an ambiguous *_SHA256 is refused, a generator PROBLEM stops the walk. Exit 0 = converged, 1 = changes made/pending, 2 = refused/PROBLEM
  tri fpga-pins FILE — the blast radius of editing FILE, before the edit: every spec pinning it by sha256 transitively (L1 direct, L2 pinners of pinners, ...) plus the params generators inside the radius — the exact set fpga-repin will then walk. Reports pin cycles (exit 1); read-only
  tri fpga-tools — every board-tool's own --self-test in one call (runlog, budget, tmpcheck, decode, repin, pins, fire, firelog), one verdict line; loopcheck runs it as its fourth component, so each fire re-verifies the whole tool layer after any edit
  tri fpga-loopstate — lint .claude/loop-state.md (read-only): sections, UART lock paragraph, exactly one fresh IN-PROGRESS row, every table fire in the fire log (live file or the firelog archive); loopcheck runs it as its fifth component, so a broken coordination file fails the sweep instead of being inherited by the next cron fire
  tri fpga-fire start "<description>" — open the NEXT fire: lock row + fire-log stub built in memory, linted, written as ONE atomic edit (the fire-18 protocol made mechanical); refuses if a fire is IN-PROGRESS or the file does not lint; numbers above the archive max too; the DONE flip and full log entry stay hand-written
  tri fpga-firelog archive — move fire-log entries whose fires lost their LOCKS rows to .claude/loop/firelog-archive.md (verbatim, never dropped; archive written first so a crash duplicates rather than loses); the linter counts a fire's entry in either home
  tri fpga-stamps | --self-test — the audit's stamp check alone: HH:MM stamps that postdate the commit that wrote them, over the claim docs, plus its calibration probe (stamp_probe steps the probe commit back across midnight so it stays inside the check's same-date scope at every instant — the fire-27 bug); in the tools self-test sweep
  tri fpga-keep PATH TAG | --self-test — keep a volatile /tmp tree durably: every file -> artifacts/model_inputs/blobs/<sha256> (gitignored) + a MANIFEST.tsv row (tracked), pins tag keep:TAG; after that tmpcheck watches the tree and --restore rebuilds it after a reboot (fire 28: the round-1 corpus had no builder, only /tmp and a stopped pod); in the tools self-test sweep
  tri fpga-derive ft_t27_8k [--out DIR] — rebuild the kept corpus from its chain (~/t27 at the pinned commit via git archive, the sibling's t27_bench.py + data.py with the held-copy patch, items/tokenizer from the keep blobs) and sha256-verify every MANIFEST.tsv row tagged keep:ft_t27_8k; 91/92 rows byte-identical, manifest.json checked on content, proven fire 29
  tri fpga-genscore CANDS.jsonl [...] [--min-lines N --pass-frac F] | --self-test — score t27_bench gen candidates for a behavioral criterion: literal >=N-line count AND degeneracy-filtered count (unique stripped lines < half the body = repetition loop, fire 35); the verdict rides the FILTERED count at --pass-frac of rows; in the tools self-test sweep
  tri fpga-jtag [--load] [--expect XC7A100T] | --decode HEX | --self-test — JTAG chain behind a Xilinx Platform Cable USB II (DLC10, 03fd): fxload only on --load (no sudo), xc3sprog -c xpc -j, each IDCODE named; no chain -> raw TDO shift classified (all ones = nothing drives TDO: VREF/ribbon/orientation; all zeros = TDO held low: cable). Never programs. Exit 0 chain, 1 none, 2 no cable
  tri fpga-seeds --parse LOG... [--csv OUT] | --run --chipdb F --xdc F --json F --seeds 1-20 --out DIR | --self-test — Fmax as a distribution over nextpnr-xilinx seeds: CSV row per seed (LUT/FF/CARRY4, post-route Fmax, logic/routing ns) + min/median/max; warns when cell counts differ; --run keeps one log per seed, refuses overwrite, writes input sha256s + nextpnr version
  tri fpga-selftest — off-board --self-test of every conformance/*.py a .t27 spec names (RUNNER or *_FILE); refuses a self_test that opens a port (exit 2 = fail/missing/refused)
  tri fpga-build --out DIR [--node N --rev REV] — build a node bitstream locally (openXC7, prjxray-db ab1fc60);
                     never touches the board, only prints the flash command (conformance/NODE_TOOLCHAIN_RESTORE.md)
  tri fpga-flash NAME BIT --owner-yes "QUOTE" [--expect SHA_PREFIX] — load a bitstream into SRAM (sudo openocd,
                     the owner types the password); refuses without the owner's quoted yes, with openocd running,
                     with an existing log or a foreign payload, or while a board run holds the UART lock (exit 75); records everything in board_runs/NAME.log; the key is wiped after a load
  tri fpga-restore NAME BIT --owner-yes "QUOTE" [--expect SHA_PREFIX] [--task ID] — the post-power-event chain
                     in one command: probe the JTAG chain (no sudo; idcode 0x13636093 = the XC7A200T answers,
                     all-ones = board power, no device = the FTDI half-enumeration wedge), then the fpga-flash
                     load, then discover_port.py for the UART (status 0x04 after a fresh load is normal: no key
                     yet), then the whole chain as one note on the task
  --- experience and skills ---
  tri learn --audit — how many memory index pointers lead to a file that does not exist
  tri learn <slug> --hook "..." --desc "..." --body-file F [--type feedback] — save experience: the file first, then the pointer
  tri skills [filter] — which skills are on disk and which have no SKILL.md of their own
  tri proof <file.md> ...  — whether what a document refers to exists (exit 2 if not)
  tri loop-lesson "text" — record a LOOP lesson in state.json and ledger.jsonl in one command,
                     at the moment of the finding (not the `lesson` command above: that one writes to loop-opus/LESSONS.md)
  tri lesson-orphans [--all] — which lessons from state.json reached NOT A SINGLE skill
                     of the trios tree (--all: plus both home skill directories; the command
                     prints which roots it read); exit 2 = orphans
  --- loop instruments that had no entry point before 2026-09-13 ---
  tri which-board [--json|--no-gh|--selftest] — which GitHub board each loop instrument reads
                     and whether it moves; exit 2 = the instruments are split (the `board` command above is different: the trios dashboard)
  tri judge-calibration --build [N] | --score FILE | --report — measure the JUDGE on questions
                     whose answer is arithmetic; exit 2 = the judge confirmed a phantom
  tri dash2 [--write] [--reading F] [--no-color] — loop dashboard from a FRESH measurement: liveness from two
                     signals, every number has an age, unmeasured shows as '-' (`cycle-dash` shows the one already drawn)
  tri help (alias: tri -h, tri --help) — this help
USAGE
